 ### Paletted Texture Normal Storage
-A storage method for lighting normals using paletted textures to save space, storing an index into a normal lookup table per voxel [S2]. Directions are quantized to one of $2^{40}$ vectors obtained from the faces of a subdivided combined dodecahedron and icosahedron [S2]. This approach requires only one byte per voxel to store normal directions, significantly reducing memory usage compared to the standard 3-byte quantized normal storage [S2]. It is chosen when memory is extremely constrained and the specific quantization grid is acceptable.
