 ## Background
-The Quantized Normal Volume Storage method was introduced in the context of interactive volume rendering using multi-dimensional transfer functions [S1]. It was developed to address the increased memory consumption needed to store transfer function variables and normals at each voxel sample point for hardware-based rendering [S1]. The Paletted Texture Normal Storage method was proposed as an alternative to save space by using paletted textures [S2].
